nt  food whether you eat at home or you eat  at a restaurant it doesn't matter you  can't hide from the inflation it's over  five percent food prices whether you eat  at home or you eat out or over five  percent according to the official  numbers transportation four and a half  apparel 4.3 and shelter  3.5 if you believe that shelters only up  3.5 i got a lot of nonsense to sell you  because that is frankly not true  so whether we believe the official  numbers or not let's just look at the  official numbers absolutely insane to  see gasoline at 50  5-0 now if you go back here is the story  around inflation charlie all over this  janet yellen specifically said february  nothing to worry about in march small  and manageable in may it is only  temporary in june could reach three  percent but it is just transitory and  then in early october it's higher for  the next several months and in late  october trillions more in spending with  lower prices so when we go ahead and we  look at this what we see is that janet  yellen and others it's not just her  economists politicians and academics  just over and over and over again  gaslighting all of the american citizens  what we saw was that they were saying  that there was nothing to worry about to  begin with then they said oh there might  be a little bit of inflation but don't  worry then it was oh there might be high  levels of inflation but it may be  transitory and now we have 6.2 percent  inflation in this country in the  official numbers and the unofficial  number is likely over 10  if you use the 1980 measure for  inflation it is likely that we are  seeing somewhere between 13 to 15  inflation in the united states it is  insane so how does this stack up against  the rest of the world maybe it's just  relative everyone's inflation has gone  up and it's not that big of a deal well  that's not true we can go ahead here and  we can look at the global inflation  rates and we look at the global  inflation rates we can see in 